<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  App-level privacy manifest (arch A2 / auditS H3). Absent, this is a
  guaranteed ITMS-91053 rejection on first App Store submission: the app calls
  a "required reason" API and every such call must be declared here.

  What was enumerated to write this, and how to re-check it (2026-08-04):

  * UserDefaults — the one required-reason API this app uses. All 20 persisted
    keys are owned by `SavedDataKey` (Sources/VinodexCore/SavedData.swift), so
    the surface is enumerable rather than grep-derived. Reason CA92.1 covers
    reading and writing defaults accessible only to the app itself — correct
    here: no app group, no extension, no shared container.
  * File timestamps (C617.1) — NOT used, checked because auditS H3 raised it
    for ProfileAvatar.swift: avatar.jpg and the SavedDataArchive export go
    through Data(contentsOf:)/write(to:)/removeItem only, and no
    creationDate/modificationDate/attributesOfItem/stat call exists anywhere
    in Sources/. Re-grep before trusting this if file handling grows.
  * System boot time, disk space, active keyboards — no call sites.

  Tracking is false and both arrays are empty because nothing leaves the
  device: no network calls at runtime, no analytics, no third-party SDK — the
  package has zero dependencies.

  Placement: this file ships at the root of Vinodex_VinodexApp.bundle via the
  `.copy` resource rule (Apple's aggregation reads app and embedded bundle
  roots; nesting it under a Resources/ subdirectory would hide it). xtool has
  no passthrough for placing files at the .app root itself — the same gap that
  keeps the Info.plist source and bundle version out of reach (auditS M6,
  arch P5) — so when a signing pipeline exists, promote this file to the .app
  bundle root alongside those. CI's `test` job fails if this file goes missing
  or stops declaring the UserDefaults category.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>CA92.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
